{"title":"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Properties of Logarithms)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Properties of Logarithms)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Properties of Logarithms)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Exponential_Form)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Exponential Form)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Guess_and_Check)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Guess and Check)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is a unique positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d23cbff85ac447661855a4f0344f9c162ce14b2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2{(\\log_{16}{n})} = \\log_4{(\\log_4{n})}.\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />What is the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28578f91569670ce8f5d1c27b4ea637a09a75a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/8/d18fbfa130861cd5b9603e7c68b2819b0e332212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 7 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 11 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"373\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Properties_of_Logarithms.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\">Solution 1 (Properties of Logarithms)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Properties of Logarithms)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1dfea0e2b465b46af20e891253b53f3ab2ff66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{a^b} c = \\frac{1}{b} \\log_a c.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" /> This can be proved by using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Change_of_base_formula\" title=\"Change of base formula\"> Change of Base Formula</a> to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef9cdc7c7d46920eac603663914e0d9261a99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p>So, the original equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1da5c39040181594aef8542683a22a284bac1d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{(\\log_{2^4}{n})} = \\log_{2^2}{(\\log_{2^2}{n})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d344b1cce4fbf03d2dcbc2bf4998068ffa5e2a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2\\left({\\frac{1}{4}\\log_{2}{n}}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}\\log_2\\left({\\frac{1}{2}\\log_2{n}}\\right).\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"43\" />\nUsing log property of addition, we expand both sides and then simplify:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c7644d56246ebaab19aa6d4f34258a94d2dcaa2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_2{\\frac{1}{4}}+\\log_2{(\\log_{2}{n}}) &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\log_2{\\frac{1}{2}} +\\log_{2}{(\\log_2{n})}\\right] \\\\ \\log_2{\\frac{1}{4}}+\\log_2{(\\log_{2}{n}}) &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}\\left[-1 +\\log_{2}{(\\log_2{n})}\\right] \\\\ -2+\\log_2{(\\log_{2}{n}}) &amp;= -\\frac{1}{2}+ \\frac{1}{2}(\\log_{2}{(\\log_2{n})}). \\end{align*}\" width=\"379\" height=\"129\" />\nSubtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/d/65dbe66555c90b3c47ebc40aa08dc572c5698444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(\\log_{2}{(\\log_2{n})})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" /> from both sides and adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to both sides gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255add85531086624dceabb0743af1e5fa785939.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}(\\log_{2}{(\\log_2{n})}) = \\frac{3}{2}.\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"37\" />\nMultiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1d1407aac4125d6c453a365eb173d96ebb48e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> exponentiating, and simplifying gives us\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/5/fc56ee53e5bced8c40923f803be8b14f4dd6639d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{2}{(\\log_2{n})} &amp;= 3 \\\\ \\log_2{n}&amp;=8 \\\\ n&amp;=256. \\end{align*}\" width=\"147\" height=\"63\" />\nAdding the digits together, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cd97663dcd92cfbd34c5800f6e1e887ffbc197.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+5+6=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" /> \n</p><p>~quacker88 (Solution)\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (Reformatting)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Properties_of_Logarithms.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\">Solution 2 (Properties of Logarithms)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Properties of Logarithms)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will apply the following logarithmic identity:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac5558c7e0481bf9449dd5cb896e0a3f292bdc5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{p^k}{q^k}=\\log_{p}{q},\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"22\" />\nwhich can be proven by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Change_of_base_formula\" title=\"Change of base formula\"> Change of Base Formula</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e039b46e7340c628409a100dbe07f8911b6fd8aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{p^k}{q^k}=\\frac{\\log_{p}{q^k}}{\\log_{p}{p^k}}=\\frac{k\\log_{p}{q}}{k}=\\log_{p}{q}.\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"47\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db29361c586c52e75a4fcd88e2e324c313fbe426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{16}{n}\\neq0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"19\" /> so we rewrite the original equation as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71df5db834e69b88e77936beb8153d9264977280.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_4{(\\log_{16}{n})^2}&amp;=\\log_4{(\\log_4{n})} \\\\ (\\log_{16}{n})^2&amp;=\\log_4{n} \\\\ (\\log_{16}{n})^2&amp;=\\log_{16}{n^2} \\\\ (\\log_{16}{n})^2&amp;=2\\log_{16}{n} \\\\ \\log_{16}{n}&amp;=2, \\end{align*}\" width=\"222\" height=\"127\" />\nfrom which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55a49bb1e79d90971139d241cb8b14d9193c941b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=16^2=256.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" /> The sum of its digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cd97663dcd92cfbd34c5800f6e1e887ffbc197.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+5+6=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Properties_of_Logarithms.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\">Solution 3 (Properties of Logarithms)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Properties of Logarithms)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the change of base formula on the RHS of the initial equation yields \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/980135a092cbde9093614175ce2c5d367dca77e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2{(\\log_{16}{n})} = \\frac{\\log_2{(\\log_4{n})}}{\\log_2{4}}.\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"43\" />\nThis means we can multiply each side by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1f38b16ef0accf9cd3084d48672f78026364f63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2{(\\log_{16}{n})^2} = \\log_2{(\\log_4{n})}.\\]\" width=\"227\" height=\"20\" />\nCanceling out the logs gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec7653c81124125a07627dbaf4c38dc2b33f46b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\log_{16}{n})^2=\\log_4{n}.\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />\nWe use change of base on the RHS to see that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34fa55e546dc6bfdddef59fb23514faa814811ef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (\\log_{16}{n})^2&amp;=\\frac{ \\log_{16}{n}}{\\log_{16}{4}} \\\\ (\\log_{16}{n})^2&amp;=2 \\log_{16}{n}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"163\" height=\"68\" />\nSubstituting in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f9848afe2dcb8f1be100e5a0cb60167c1104159f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\log_{16}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"19\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d48524d20baf121feb256b60b48dc0c5ac972b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2=2m,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4797950b5e812b65381cbc5fc33ad2db5f57aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e275495e7e44d279fb3e5051b3a63115e79ead5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> yields no solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> (since this would lead to use taking the log of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/045aa826bcb4d6ceb9a17d62b8d3be38b25eb7e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 = \\log_{16}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"19\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a28ad14d5bc7ba927455ddab603d464379e7cb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=16^2=256,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" /> for the digit-sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f39a10825c7b89957a61a7001cfa4a6f7e49de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 5 + 6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~aop2014\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Exponential_Form.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Exponential_Form)\">Solution 4 (Exponential Form)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Exponential Form)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e000d0af4d0ea6d548b571e28be085a13992ab0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\log_{16}n)=k\\implies\\log_{16}n=2^k\\implies n=16^{2^k}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"398\" height=\"25\" /> Similarly, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed32b4848486778b2a8ff6704cde49f28571f79d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_4(\\log_4 n)=k\\implies \\log_4 n=4^k\\implies n=4^{4^k}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"375\" height=\"25\" /> Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11a51d99e1a0645dacaa922d362c286f8f99f902.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16^{2^k}=(4^2)^{2^k}=4^{2^{k+1}}\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/932234b759d70e8ebeaac843237349f46b8460b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4^{4^k}=4^{2^{2k}},\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"22\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a415de7800ec70e311555e142a5f012e9b2cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1=2k\\implies k=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"184\" height=\"16\" /> Plugging this in to either one of the expressions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd678361b0f40ec2723283c0f2bab3df5cadc68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, and the requested answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cd97663dcd92cfbd34c5800f6e1e887ffbc197.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+5+6=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Guess_and_Check.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Guess_and_Check)\">Solution 5 (Guess and Check)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Guess and Check)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that, as the answer is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be some power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7a897ec83c3783ee1d996c0bd0f6d70ac8bd52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> Testing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b99dab4636826e5cf13220eeb6949ef52aa1be8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_2{(\\log_{16}{16})} &amp;= \\log_4{(\\log_4{16})} \\\\ \\log_2{1} &amp;= \\log_4{2} \\\\ 0 &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}, \\end{align*}\" width=\"229\" height=\"87\" />\nwhich does not work. We then try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972ad1bf6cf4ae9dcefdf2be3bcc1f74c99ba676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$256,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> giving us\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f4ee015652dc93368ff65a1e7f464d1bb443b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_2{(\\log_{16}{256})} &amp;= \\log_4{(\\log_4{256})} \\\\ \\log_2{2} &amp;= \\log_4{4} \\\\ 1 &amp;= 1, \\end{align*}\" width=\"247\" height=\"67\" />\nwhich holds true. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/9/02942f5bd944f82364c22369767ef919025cb456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 256,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f39a10825c7b89957a61a7001cfa4a6f7e49de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 5 + 6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>(Don't use this technique unless you absolutely need to! Guess and check methods aren't helpful for learning math.)\n</p><p>~ciceronii (Solution)\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (Reformatting)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fzZzGqNqW6U\">https://youtu.be/fzZzGqNqW6U</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RdIIEhsbZKw?t=814\">https://youtu.be/RdIIEhsbZKw?t=814</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/EnyzIHcJ8Aw\">https://youtu.be/EnyzIHcJ8Aw</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A\">2020 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?t